<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20967] 'failure_domain' file does not create name for itself</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20967</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Newly formatted OSTs return an e2fsck error about unattached inode 88 repeatedly:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;e2fsck 1.47.3-wc2 (11-Nov-2025)
Pass 1: Checking inodes, blocks, and sizes
Pass 2: Checking directory structure
Pass 3: Checking directory connectivity
Pass 4: Checking reference counts
Unattached inode 88
Connect to /lost+found? no

Pass 5: Checking group summary information

myfs-OST0003: ********** WARNING: Filesystem still has errors **********

myfs-OST0003: 629/4294160640 files (0.2% non-contiguous), 537388688/4879024128 blocks
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This inode is supposed to point at the &lt;tt&gt;failure_domain&lt;/tt&gt; file which was added in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19066" title="FLR2: identify rack/PSU failure domains for servers" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19066"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19066&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Running &lt;tt&gt;debugfs&lt;/tt&gt; shows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;#  debugfs -c -R "ls -l /" /dev/nvme1n10 | cat
debugfs 1.47.3-wc2 (11-Nov-2025)
      2   40755 (2)      0      0    4096  7-Oct-2026 16:49 .
      2   40755 (2)      0      0    4096  7-Oct-2026 16:49 ..

      87  100644 (1)      0      0       0  1-Jan-1970 00:00 health_check

      89  100644 (1)      0      0    8192  1-Jan-1970 00:00 nodemap
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and &lt;tt&gt;health_check&lt;/tt&gt; was created immediately before &lt;tt&gt;failure_domain&lt;/tt&gt; in &lt;tt&gt;ofd_fs_setup()&lt;/tt&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;        lu_local_obj_fid(&amp;amp;info-&amp;gt;fti_fid, OFD_HEALTH_CHECK_OID);
        memset(&amp;amp;info-&amp;gt;fti_attr, 0, sizeof(info-&amp;gt;fti_attr));
        info-&amp;gt;fti_attr.la_valid = LA_MODE;
        info-&amp;gt;fti_attr.la_mode = S_IFREG | 0644;
        info-&amp;gt;fti_dof.dof_type = dt_mode_to_dft(S_IFREG);

        fo = dt_find_or_create(env, ofd-&amp;gt;ofd_osd, &amp;amp;info-&amp;gt;fti_fid,
                               &amp;amp;info-&amp;gt;fti_dof, &amp;amp;info-&amp;gt;fti_attr);
        if (IS_ERR(fo))
                GOTO(out_seqs, rc = PTR_ERR(fo));

        ofd-&amp;gt;ofd_health_check_file = fo;

        lu_local_obj_fid(&amp;amp;info-&amp;gt;fti_fid, OFD_FAILURE_DOMAIN_OID);
        fd = dt_find_or_create(env, ofd-&amp;gt;ofd_osd, &amp;amp;info-&amp;gt;fti_fid,
                               &amp;amp;info-&amp;gt;fti_dof, &amp;amp;info-&amp;gt;fti_attr);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is no entry for &lt;tt&gt;failure_domain&lt;/tt&gt; in &lt;tt&gt;osd_lf_maps[]&lt;/tt&gt; in &lt;tt&gt;osd_scrub.c&lt;/tt&gt; since no name is defined for &lt;tt&gt;failure_domain&lt;/tt&gt; file. e2fsck pass 4 name linkage treats it as disconnected and will reconnect it in &lt;tt&gt;lost+found&lt;/tt&gt;, which might accidentally be deleted by an admin at some point in the future, and e2fsck errors are always a concern for admins so they should be avoided.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
